we've reviewed a lot of smaller more  compact headphones on this channel  lately now it's time for one of the  industry's best beats by dre studio  Wireless threes what's going on guys my  name is David Tommy and welcome back to  the channel today as I previously  mentioned we're reviewing the beats by  dre studio Wireless threes more  specifically we're reviewing the matte  black version of the wireless threes if  you guys love the matte black headphones  make sure you check out the link down  below to one of my companies called wire  watches we've recently launched a whole  collection of midnight black watches  that I know you guys are gonna love  alright so let's talk about these  headphones right here I've had these  headphones for just over a year now and  I used to use them every single day for  video editing work and sometimes going  to the gym as well to be perfectly  honest with you guys it's the second  pair of beats by dre as I've owned the  last couple years recently I just got  rid of my studio twos and upgraded to  the studio threes thinking that unlike  my studio twos I'd use them a lot more  and in fact I did when I first got these  headphones I use them all the time  but as time went on I stopped using them  as much and I think that's part of the  reason I'm making this review so if  you're in Australia like me you're  looking at paying about $450 for these  headphones full price at a store like JB  hi-fi you can pick them up for a little  bit cheaper when they're on sale but  they don't go on sale too often as they  are controlled by Apple this video isn't  sponsored anyway so it is completely my  genuine opinion about these headphones  over the time I've been using them I  loved them at the start they were great  and there was absolutely nothing wrong  with them the sound quality was  incredible the bass was so powerful and  just the clarity and the richness of the  tones was amazing it was definitely  worth the price I paid for them but over  time I actually stopped using them as  much I just started using the standard  desktop speakers that are hidden behind  the fake little plant there and these  things just kind of sat on my desk for a  while and I think one of the main  reasons for that was the fact when when  you put them on after a while being in  Australia it does get very hot now again  you started to sweat underneath the  cuffs and it got really  really irritating and the top of your  head started to get a little bit sore  and after editing for two three four  hours straight but these headphones kind  of got a little bit uncomfortable in my  personal opinion and that's why I found  it so much easier just to edit straight  from the desktop speakers yes I know I'm  compromising a little bit of sound  quality but for a peace of mind and  could just practicality and comfort that  was worth it for me one thing I found  that with these headphones is the little  leather ear cups do occasionally get a  little bit sweaty and stinky and gross  so with my studio twos that I mentioned  before I used to wear them to the gym  every single day and after a while well  the leather earpieces just kind of got  really stinking and gross so I had to go  online order a second pair replace the  little cuffs but they were never the  same so the end of the day I ended up  with $450 headphones that didn't feel  like a premium brand and smelt a little  bit not exactly ideal especially if  you're considering buying these  headphones for the gym or any other  physical exercise that you get a sweat  during there is one more little con  about these headphones and one of the  main reasons I did buy them was the fact  when I travel I usually put these big  headphones on because little in-ear ones  get really uncomfortable on a plane and  they start hurting my ears quite a lot  so I thought that if I buy these  headphones they're gonna be perfect for  travel and I'm gonna be able to throw my  backpack all the time and just not worry  about them I guess there's technology  advanced and things got better  the little Samsung buds for example  became my primary go-to headphones even  on plane trips now they aren't as  irritating and they're much better and  much more comfortable to wear then old  any headphones used to be so yeah  originally I thought I was gonna be able  to travel with these headphones and just  have them in my backpack all the time  but as my backpack got heavier with more  and more camera gear and different  accessories and different lenses the  space in my camera bag got less and less  and less so eventually these headphones  actually ended up staying in the  cupboard instead of coming with me  overseas unfortunately that was a big  shortfall for me and that's one of the  reasons I think I've decided to step  away from these headphones and move  forward into the brand  dancing buds that's just my personal  opinion and my personal choice for my  lifestyle because I believe they're more  practical and more powerful for me in an  everyday situation they're lugging these  things around from portability  perspective I've given you a bunch of  cons here but realistically these  headphones are still incredible pieces  of engineering and they do an a  magnificent job if you are in the market  for something like these don't be afraid  to actually go out and buy them I know  there has been a little bit of chatter  online about these headphones recently  predominantly about the fact that it's a  bit of an outdated design that's a  little bit big clunky and a little bit  chunky as well but firstly speaking from  somebody who studied architecture and  spends most of their day designing I  still genuinely love these headphones  I think the map that color is what gets  me from day dot when you see them in the  shops and when you see them in real life  there are completely different beasts to  anything out there the fact that they  have such a premium feel and aesthetic  to them really gets you over the line  now I know this is a superficial way of  thinking about a product and it's more  about the quality of the sound that it  puts out but the looks do play a part  when you're selecting your perfect  headphones even during the unboxing  experience they've really gone to the  details and made sure that matte or  matte black finish has been carried out  throughout the whole design so overall  what do I really think about these  headphones I think they're an amazing  set of headphones that are going to give  you that premium sound all rich base  that you're probably looking for if  you're checking out this video however I  do think they're a little bit chunky I  do think they're a little bit big and  not very practical and portable I do  think they're a little bit overpriced  and you're paying for that beats by dre  premium price tag which at the end of  the day for the sound quality producers  I do think it's justified they are very  durable headphones that I personally  believe are gonna last your lifetime if  you take care of them however if you're  planning on using these headphones to go  to the gym or do anything that's gonna  cause you to sweat whilst wearing them  you may have a few problems down the  track so make sure that if you are  sweating in them take them out of the  box when you get home clean them off let  them to air out and hopefully you won't  have the same problems I had before so  if you're looking for a pair of  headphones to sit on your desk and you  as a workhorse these are probably the  ones I would recommend however if you  are looking for something it's simply a  little bit more portable practical and  that you're gonna use every day I would  suggest that you take a look into  Samsung buds or the Apple earpods these  are the things that are going to get you  through the day in the most comfortable  and most convenient way possible for you  right now in 2019 and that's all I have  for you guys today the video was short  and sharp and I hope you enjoyed it and  make sure you smash that subscribe  button the channel is growing thank you  so much for being a part of it and as  always I'll see you next Monday for  another tech review or e-commerce  related adventure

